{#-
  BLOCK: table — §06's `table`. The five-column listings table with a
  brand-coloured header.

  Moved verbatim from `_build_sales_table`. Row values are shaped in Python and
  arrive here already formatted: this block decides nothing about what a price
  or a spec string looks like, only where it goes. That split is deliberate —
  `_format_price_clean` and the status-badge palette are tested in Python, and a
  template is a bad place to hide either.

  TWO COLOUR ROLES, AND THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. The header cells sit ON the
  brand fill and take `on_header`; the price column is brand-coloured text on a
  white or near-white row and takes `price_ink`. Hardcoding `#ffffff` for the
  first and the raw accent for the second put five header labels at 1.98:1 on
  lime and every price at 3.74:1 on Luxury Estates.
-#}
              <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="margin-bottom: 24px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden;">
                <tr>
                  <td style="background: {{ primary_color }}; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: {{ on_header }}; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;">Address</td>
                  <td style="background: {{ primary_color }}; padding: 12px 10px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: {{ on_header }}; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-align: center;">Bd/Ba</td>
                  <td style="background: {{ primary_color }}; padding: 12px 10px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: {{ on_header }}; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-align: right;">Sq Ft</td>
                  <td style="background: {{ primary_color }}; padding: 12px 10px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: {{ on_header }}; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-align: right;">Price</td>
                  <td style="background: {{ primary_color }}; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: {{ on_header }}; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-align: center;">DOM</td>
                </tr>
                {% for r in rows %}
                        <tr>
                          <td style="background: {{ r.bg }}; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #334155; {{ r.border }}">{{ r.address }}{{ r.badge_html }}</td>
                          <td style="background: {{ r.bg }}; padding: 12px 10px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #475569; text-align: center; {{ r.border }}">{{ r.specs }}</td>
                          <td style="background: {{ r.bg }}; padding: 12px 10px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #475569; text-align: right; {{ r.border }}">{{ r.sqft }}</td>
                          <td style="background: {{ r.bg }}; padding: 12px 10px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: {{ price_ink }}; text-align: right; {{ r.border }}">{{ r.price }}</td>
                          <td style="background: {{ r.bg }}; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #475569; text-align: center; {{ r.border }}">{{ r.dom }}</td>
                        </tr>
                {%- endfor %}
              </table>
